# PENDING-CONVERSION (must be gone before v0.1.18)
# Timers that break the rule (write, release, route, commit or re-ask on a clock). The default run
# warns for each; `--strict` (release tier) fails on any. Delete a line when its timer is gone.
app/src/ai/blocklist/agent_view/controller.rs	ENTER_OR_EXIT_CONFIRMATION_WINDOW	FOUND: 1 s double-press window; once it lapses the pending enter/exit-agent-view confirmation is cleared, so the clock decides what the second key does (UI confirmation; owner may exempt)
app/src/ai/blocklist/inline_action/ask_user_question_view.rs	ASK_USER_QUESTION_AUTO_ADVANCE_DELAY	FOUND: after a single-select answer a timer CONFIRMS it (AskUserQuestionAction::Confirm) unless the user navigates (commits on a clock)
crates/warp_tui/src/tui_ask_question_view.rs	AUTO_ADVANCE_DELAY	FOUND: 300 ms timer auto-confirms a single-select answer in the TUI (commits on a clock)
crates/warp_tui/src/terminal_session_view.rs	CTRL_C_EXIT_WINDOW	FOUND: double-^C window; the clock decides whether a second ^C exits / kills the child agent (UI confirmation; owner may exempt)
app/src/terminal/local_tty/terminal_attributes.rs	POLL_INTERVAL	FOUND: 1 Hz termios poll (a re-ask on a clock) feeding the password / interactive-prompt detector that hands the command to the user
app/src/terminal/local_tty/terminal_manager.rs	judge	FOUND: quiet timer armed from PromptDetector::next_wake; firing runs the prompt detection that hands the command over (INTERACTIVE_PROMPT_QUIET_*)
app/src/terminal/local_tty/terminal_manager.rs	observe	FOUND: quiet timer armed from the stall detector; firing can send q to a pager or hand the command over (STALL_*)
app/src/terminal/model/block.rs	wakeup_after_delay	UNVERIFIED: delay after preexec, then the interactive latch settles and the probe is consulted about who owns the terminal (input state decided after a clock; the probe decides, the timer schedules)
app/src/terminal/local_tty/event_loop.rs	REPLY_GATE_POLL	FOUND: 10 ms poll that re-checks the pty mode and then WRITES withheld terminal-query replies (app protocol bytes, not user keys)
app/src/terminal/local_tty/event_loop.rs	REPLY_GATE_POLL_SLOW	FOUND: 100 ms back-off of the same reply-gate poll
app/src/terminal/local_tty/event_loop.rs	REPLY_GATE_SLOW_AFTER	FOUND: 1 s after which the reply-gate poll slows down

# PACING (owner-exempt 2026-11-09: our own bootstrap bytes into a relay/container/cooked tty whose consumption is unobservable, #960 #1384; never user keys)
# Each needs a `pacing: <why>` comment next to it; the guard fails if its code path mentions a user-key API. Not counted by --strict.
app/src/terminal/writeable_pty/pty_controller.rs	RELAY_BOOTSTRAP_PACING	25 ms gap between chunks of our own bootstrap into a user-space pty relay (#960)
app/src/terminal/writeable_pty/pty_controller.rs	CONTAINER_BOOTSTRAP_PACING	50 ms gap between chunks of our own bootstrap into a container exec proxy (#960)
app/src/terminal/writeable_pty/pty_controller.rs	MAC_TTY_INPUT_QUEUE_PACING	10 ms gap between chunks of our own ssh-warpify payload on a cooked tty (#1384)
app/src/terminal/writeable_pty/pty_controller.rs	write_next_paced_chunk	timer chain writing the next chunk of an app-built paced payload (bootstrap / warpify), never user keys
